    { q: 'Why does a tiled floor feel colder than a rug at the same temperature?', a: ['Tiles conduct heat away from your foot faster', 'Tiles really are colder', 'The rug radiates heat into you'], c: 0, why: 'They are the same temperature. The tile is just a better conductor, so it takes your heat quicker.' }
